;; spec:   syntax §4.3, types §2.11 (compiler.md section 5)
;; expect: trap
;; trap:   boom
;; `trap` has any type, so it can stand where a value is needed; the
;; program aborts before the `+` ever runs. The compiler lowered the
;; `+` and the return after the call that does not return, into code
;; nothing reaches, which lIR refuses when it uses a name bound there
;; (lir.md §5); it now discards what follows a jump. Found with case
;; 172's division by a literal zero, the same shape.
(defun main () -> i64 (+ 1 (trap "boom")))
